WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:04.790
Inazuma Eleven GO is about to start!

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:12.760
Raimon...

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.940
Holy Emperor, you have a visitor.

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.920
It's been a long time.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:29.160
Hamano!

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:30.850
Got it!

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:31.880
Now!

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:34.670
Try again next time!

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:36.400
Kageyama!

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.960
You need to predict the opponent's movements!

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:43.500
It's not like they'll just stay still and wait for you to steal the ball!

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:44.350
Okay!

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:46.310
Here he comes.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.020
Don't think you'll get the better of me!

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:50.390
This way!

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:55.320
Amagi-senpai!

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:58.030
Y-You're pretty good.

00:02:58.630 --> 00:02:59.540
Kageyama!

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:03.910
I won't let you through!

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:07.490
Hayami!

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.160
They're all in great condition.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:14.210
Coach Kidou's training menu to build up their basic physical power is really working.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:16.750
Amagi, pick up the pace!

00:03:23.250 --> 00:03:24.500
We'll get it this time!

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:25.290
Yeah!

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:33.540
Kaboom...

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:34.750
Jump!

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:47.950
Looks like they still have a way to go over here.

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.460
It's that name that needs fixing.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:53.540
Who the heck named it "Kaboom Jump"?!

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.130
Did I catch a cold?

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:08.340
Something on your mind?

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:11.060
Just remembering the past.

00:04:11.510 --> 00:04:12.770
Remembering the past?

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:18.360
Not long ago, we were always holding back our passion.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:23.240
Even if we played the soccer we like, we couldn't be fully content with it.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:26.800
But ever since he joined, everything's changed.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:34.410
A lot's happened.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:39.600
<i>There is no soccer here!{ep 4}</i>

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.590
<i>Having scores set from the very beginning...{ep 6}</i>

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:45.420
<i>That's not soccer!</i>

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.220
<i>What would you know?!</i>

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:52.430
<i>I think that goal we made in the Eito match is really important!{ep 8}</i>

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:54.970
<i>Really important...</i>

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.690
<i>Stop trying to steal soccer from us!{ep 11}</i>

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:01.190
<i>Steal from you?</i>

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:03.320
<i>I just want to play real soccer...</i>

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.080
<i>Quit? Are you serious?</i>

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:08.740
<i>Yeah, I can't play along with this anymore.</i>

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:14.160
<i>The reason why I came back to Raimon is because...</i>

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.850
<i>I'm going to take down Fifth Sector.</i>

00:05:19.950 --> 00:05:24.870
With our goal set on this revolution, everyone's hearts have become one.

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:26.380
Kirino.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.680
Soccer sure is great.

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:31.450
Shindou...

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:33.810
Yeah!

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:35.910
Get moving!

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:37.060
Okay!

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:40.860
I've got that!

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:43.150
Nishiki-senpai!

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:45.360
You're not getting through!

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:46.740
Now!

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:55.220
Did you see that just now?

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:55.970
Yeah!

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:59.340
That's so impressive that he can keep the ball in possession in that position!

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:00.210
Yeah!

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:01.790
Hey, you two!

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:03.710
Sorry, sorry!

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.800
Is that the attitude you give to someone who's helping you out?

00:06:11.540 --> 00:06:13.560
Whoa, what's that? Awesome!

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:22.810
Sorry, sorry!

00:06:23.980 --> 00:06:26.960
All right, that's enough for today's practice.

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:35.260
Coach Kidou's practice menu really works me out.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:37.120
I'm all tired out too.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:41.060
Nishiki, your technique has gotten really consistent.

00:06:41.060 --> 00:06:42.910
You must've trained a lot overseas.

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:45.740
Naw, I've still got a ways!

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.510
Well, I'll be off now.

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:51.740
Nishiki-senpai!

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:55.090
Tell us about your days in Italy!

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:58.280
What's soccer like in Italy?

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:00.190
Is it really different?

00:07:01.030 --> 00:07:02.900
Italy's soccer?

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:06.110
It's like pasta.

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:08.980
Pasta?

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.330
You mean like spaghetti?

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:13.570
What do you mean?

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:16.540
Well, just think about it some.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:25.760
Pasta, eh...

00:07:25.760 --> 00:07:27.360
What do you think he means?

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:29.560
Pasta...

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:30.800
Pasta, right?

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:36.930
So it's long, soft, like the Napolitan kind we have at home a lot...

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:39.390
There's carbonara and vongole, too!

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:42.050
Yeah. And that spicy kind...

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:45.140
What was it? Penpera... No...

00:07:45.140 --> 00:07:47.330
Perapera...

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:48.470
Peperoncino!

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:50.280
Yeah, that's it!

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:53.350
But isn't that all still spaghetti?

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:56.760
He said pasta, right?

00:07:56.760 --> 00:08:00.160
Then there's fettuccine and penne too.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:01.390
Penne?

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:04.010
You know, that short one with pointy tips.

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:05.110
Oh...

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:06.800
There's also conchiglie, farfalle, fusilli...

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:07.790
There's also conchiglie, farfalle, fusilli...

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:08.870
There's also conchiglie, farfalle, fusilli...

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.870
Even if you just say pasta, there are all sorts to consider.

00:08:12.870 --> 00:08:14.870
I-I see...

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:16.730
Oh, I get it now!

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:18.180
You do?

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:21.730
Yeah, Italy's soccer is like pasta!

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:24.130
In other words, there isn't any single way to describe it!

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:28.250
So that's what it meant!

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:30.610
Since you can't say it in just one way, it's like pasta!

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:34.180
You really do learn great things when you go to Italy!

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:38.490
Is that really the case?

00:08:50.770 --> 00:08:52.760
I'll master this for sure!

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:05.010
I missed.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:06.100
One more time!

00:09:24.550 --> 00:09:28.150
He's trying to hit that blue mark?

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:37.770
See you later! I'm going for a run!

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.510
I won't lose to Kariya.

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:47.520
I've got my pride as a third-year.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:50.480
I'm taking back my regulars seat!

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:01.490
The next opponent has been decided.

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:07.760
It's Kidokawa Seishuu.

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:10.020
Kidokawa Seishuu?!

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:11.800
So it's come.

00:10:12.030 --> 00:10:12.630
Yeah.

00:10:15.080 --> 00:10:18.700
Hey, is Kidokawa Seishuu a really strong place or something?

00:10:19.690 --> 00:10:21.700
You don't know Kidokawa Seishuu?

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:23.860
Nope, not at all.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:27.320
They're not just strong, they're super famous among the famous soccer schools!

00:10:27.320 --> 00:10:32.260
They won against Raimon in the finals last year and took the Holy Road's championship!

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:33.690
Really?!

00:10:33.900 --> 00:10:35.220
They won?

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:37.930
Wouldn't that be because of Fifth Sector's orders?

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:40.210
That match was different.

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:45.730
That time, the results for the Holy Emperor election were already in.

00:10:45.730 --> 00:10:47.790
There wasn't a score order for that match.

00:10:48.470 --> 00:10:51.160
We lost in a serious faceoff.

00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:56.610
The final match of Holy Road's Nationals tournament!

00:10:56.610 --> 00:11:03.480
Who will stand at the top of JHS soccer, the famous Raimon Jr. High or the ever-capable Kidokawa Seishuu?!

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:04.790
Raimon comes up with the ball!

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:08.630
Kidokawa's Kishibe and Raimon's Shindou!

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:10.600
It's a tough fight for the ball!

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:15.400
Kishibe steals the ball!

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:18.900
He's good.

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:27.880
They're that strong?

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:31.870
But it might be easier than you think this year.

00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:39.300
We looked into it a bit...

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:42.800
Who cares about a revolution? What a waste of time.

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:44.260
Waste of time?

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.380
Yeah, it's a waste of time.

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:48.500
What do they hope to gain from that?

00:11:48.500 --> 00:11:52.810
As long as we do as we're told, we'll get scouted for the pro youth league.

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:56.230
Jr. high school soccer is just a stepping stone.

00:11:56.880 --> 00:12:01.400
So you don't feel <i>anything</i>  when you see Raimon play soccer, Nii-san?

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:04.700
You don't wish you could play <i>real</i>  soccer?

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:06.690
Captain...

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:09.700
Then I'll tell you the truth.

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:11.710
You're just being bitter.

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:16.730
Since you can't be a regular with your own skills, you're putting the blame on Fifth Sector.

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:19.930
Hit it right on the nose, didn't I?

00:12:20.770 --> 00:12:22.400
Now you've said it!

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:23.020
Sousuke!

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:24.800
Try saying that again!

00:12:24.800 --> 00:12:26.200
What's that about me?!

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:28.300
Hey, say it again!

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:33.390
In other words, their teamwork is unstable?

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:40.870
Well, however you put it, that makes the match easy!

00:12:40.870 --> 00:12:44.200
Even if it's Kidokawa, you can't win when you're like that.

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:46.560
Will it really be that easy?

00:12:46.940 --> 00:12:48.120
What do you mean?

00:12:49.900 --> 00:12:57.660
As you all know, Kidokawa Seishuu works strongly under the influence of Fifth Sector.

00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:01.530
If we were to win against Kidokawa Seishuu as they are...

00:13:02.100 --> 00:13:04.400
We'll land a big one for the revolution!

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:09.430
Fifth Sector won't just sit back and let that happen.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:20.370
<i>As long as we do as we're told, we'll get scouted for the pro youth league.</i>

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:26.740
Even though Sousuke says that, he loves soccer just as much as his brother.

00:13:33.100 --> 00:13:35.280
What should I do...

00:13:36.700 --> 00:13:39.670
Is this the way to Kidokawa Seishuu?

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:48.330
12.23. Inazuma Eleven GO!

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:53.330
12.23. Inazuma Eleven GO!

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:05.350
Kishibe...

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:08.580
Shindou!

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:15.950
Concentrate on practice!

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:18.490
We have something to accomplish!

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:22.130
You're not getting past me!

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:23.970
Got it!

00:14:31.090 --> 00:14:32.010
Shinsuke!

00:14:32.010 --> 00:14:32.930
Yeah!

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:41.330
Kaboom...

00:14:41.540 --> 00:14:42.460
Jump!

00:14:43.510 --> 00:14:44.480
Did they do it?

00:14:50.540 --> 00:14:51.760
Ow, ow...

00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:54.390
That was great until we got to the end!

00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:55.100
Yeah!

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:56.480
All right!

00:14:56.480 --> 00:14:58.450
Kariya! One more time!

00:15:09.150 --> 00:15:10.380
I'm off!

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:12.660
Tenma, good luck!

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:13.430
Yeah!

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:19.540
It's finally the time to face Kidokawa.

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:22.060
We'll get our revenge from last year!

00:15:24.430 --> 00:15:26.830
What kind of stadium will it be this time?

00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:28.190
I can't wait to find out!

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:28.920
Yeah!

00:15:29.540 --> 00:15:30.360
Move it!

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:48.590
What was that look?

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:52.720
It was as if he's ready to risk everything on this match without hesitation.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:02.060
Aphrodi!

00:16:03.070 --> 00:16:04.310
Aphrodi?

00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:08.150
He's one of the strongest players who ever fought against Raimon!

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:27.790
Why? Why are you here?

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:32.570
Are you one of the believers of Fifth Sector's managed soccer?

00:16:53.430 --> 00:16:57.220
The third match in Holy Road, Raimon Jr. High versus Kidokawa Seishuu!

00:16:57.220 --> 00:17:00.870
The match will take place in Water World Stadium!

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:07.020
So this is the stadium this time...

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:09.710
Let's go.

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:13.920
Let's go.

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:24.640
It's steadier than I thought it'd be.

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:26.810
This'll be easy compared to that ice field.

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:30.350
Water World Stadium.

00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:32.030
What's the hidden trick in this one?

00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:40.630
It'll be all right.

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:43.410
I won't have to worry about watching my step while dribbling on this.

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:47.360
I'm announcing the starting lineup!

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:50.730
Forwards: Tsurugi, Kurama.

00:17:51.410 --> 00:17:54.670
Midfielders: Shindou, Hamano, Nishiki, Matsukaze!

00:17:56.030 --> 00:17:58.990
Defenders: Nishizono, Kariya.

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:03.430
Kurumada, Kirino.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:06.760
Goalkeeper: Sangoku. That's all.

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:13.290
He took me off.

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:15.530
He took me off...

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:17.560
Amagi...

00:18:22.580 --> 00:18:25.480
Both teams are in position!

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:29.620
The third match in the Holy Road Nationals tournament is the same as last year's finals match,

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:32.150
Kidokawa Seishuu versus Raimon Jr. High!

00:18:32.150 --> 00:18:34.700
Last year, Kidokawa won 2-1!

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:37.170
Will Raimon get their revenge?

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:41.180
The match will begin momentarily!

00:18:42.170 --> 00:18:43.350
Here we go!

00:18:45.230 --> 00:18:47.640
Guys, good luck out there!

00:18:48.430 --> 00:18:51.200
Why was I taken off the starting lineup?

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:55.610
I worked hard like everyone else with Coach Kidou's training menu!

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:57.900
But why only me?

00:18:58.320 --> 00:18:59.780
We're counting on you, Kishibe!

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:03.950
Face me, Shindou!

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:09.410
Nii-san...

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:15.440
The match starts with Raimon's kickoff!

00:19:15.790 --> 00:19:17.750
We won't lose to the likes of you!

00:19:18.190 --> 00:19:18.840
Shindou!

00:19:19.470 --> 00:19:20.310
Nishiki!

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:21.380
Tenma!

00:19:21.560 --> 00:19:24.180
Raimon makes their way up with passes!

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:26.850
Matsukaze runs ahead!

00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:28.600
You're not getting through!

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:31.980
The ball has been stolen from Matsukaze!

00:19:34.220 --> 00:19:37.460
He stole the ball from Tenma?

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:38.940
They really are strong.

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:41.890
But it's still a broken team!

00:19:41.890 --> 00:19:42.690
It's mine!

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:43.780
Izumi!

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:46.070
I won't let you through!

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:47.540
Ooisokawa!

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:52.280
Kidokawa Seishuu makes impressive passes and keeps the ball in possession!

00:19:52.490 --> 00:19:53.810
What's going on here?

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:56.310
I thought they were fighting amongst themselves!

00:19:56.310 --> 00:19:57.500
Yeah, we were.

00:19:58.510 --> 00:20:00.180
But things are different now.

00:20:00.180 --> 00:20:04.010
We're not fighting for either Fifth Sector or the revolution now.

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:06.720
We're fighting for <i>ourselves!</i>

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:17.270
When the Holy Emperor requested that I become Kidokawa Seishuu's coach,

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:19.460
the team was on the verge of falling apart.

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:27.240
Move it!

00:20:31.210 --> 00:20:33.090
I'll get you for that!

00:20:34.110 --> 00:20:37.770
At that rate, they would've been destroyed by soccer.

00:20:37.770 --> 00:20:40.460
Fifth Sector and the revolution had nothing to do with it.

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:43.200
I wanted to save them.

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:47.610
Defeat Raimon!

00:20:48.540 --> 00:20:51.520
Win and you'll be able to see the path you should continue on!

00:20:57.550 --> 00:20:58.500
Kishibe!

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:03.500
Kishibe heads up!

00:21:03.890 --> 00:21:04.950
You're not getting past us!

00:21:06.550 --> 00:21:08.260
He got past Raimon!

00:21:12.650 --> 00:21:13.450
Sousuke!

00:21:14.310 --> 00:21:17.030
Kidokawa Seishuu makes a pass!

00:21:17.310 --> 00:21:19.210
He's completely free!

00:21:19.530 --> 00:21:20.780
Sangoku-san!

00:21:21.600 --> 00:21:22.880
It's ours!

00:21:26.580 --> 00:21:27.430
What?!

00:23:08.990 --> 00:23:11.720
How are we supposed to play on a field on top of water?

00:23:11.720 --> 00:23:14.240
The destined fight between coaches has begun!

